# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Visual / Audio / World Overhaul 01 (VAWO01)
#
# The workstream authorised by the owner on 2026-09-01, which reopened PixelLab
# (10,000 generations, Tier 3) and amended `DECISIONS/0029`'s "no generation in
# this workstream" clause. Recorded in `DECISIONS/0030`.
#
# Everything below is a packaging SOURCE. `Scripts/art/package-art.js --check`
# and the UI frame kit both read from these directories, so a clean checkout
# without them fails verification -- the exact latent defect that shipped once
# already (`PIXELLAB_ASSET_INVENTORY.md` §2), and precondition P-5 of
# `GAME_BIBLE/ART/PIXELLAB_UI_PRODUCTION_PLAN.md`.
#
# `rejected/` is tracked on purpose. A rejected roll with a written verdict is
# the evidence the next round is built on, and re-learning a rejection costs
# generations (M-05).
#
# NOT tracked, deliberately: `raw/` (unselected candidate dumps) and any
# reference imagery. `WALKSCAPE_REFERENCE_SET/` remains excluded above -- it is
# third-party material and publishing it required a history rewrite (M-08).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/VAWO01/out/**
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/VAWO01/src/**
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/VAWO01/tools/**
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/VAWO01/review/**
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/VAWO01/rejected/**
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/VAWO01/*.json
GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/VAWO01/raw/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WalkScape reference set — the .md files too
#
# The images here have been excluded since M-08. The *prose* was not: the
# blanket `!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/**/*.md` exception above un-ignores
# `README.md` and `OBSERVATION_05.md`, and those describe third-party
# screenshots in construction detail. `README.md`'s own header reads
# `DO NOT COMMIT`.
#
# This is the same class of near-miss as M-08 itself: a broad exception that
# was right for round records reaching one directory it should never reach.
# Re-ignored here, after the exception, so last-match-wins puts it back.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/WALKSCAPE_REFERENCE_SET/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AUDIO/evaluation — 652 MB of audition material, never committed, and until
# now not ignored either
#
# The largest live G-8 hazard in the tree: a single `git add AUDIO/` would
# publish ~200 files including 26 MB raw WAV renders and 56 MB zips. It has
# survived this long only because every commit so far named its paths.
#
# Ignored wholesale, with exceptions for the three small classes that are
# genuinely repository knowledge — generation provenance, the mastering tools,
# and the round indices — so that re-auditioning the 40+ already-paid-for
# candidates in VAWO01 can be recorded without dragging the renders in.
# Whether those exceptions are actually taken up is an owner call
# (`FOUNDATION_L_PACKAGING.md`); the ignore is not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AUDIO/evaluation/**
!AUDIO/evaluation/**/
!AUDIO/evaluation/**/provenance/*.json
!AUDIO/evaluation/**/tools/*.mjs
!AUDIO/evaluation/INDEX*.md
!AUDIO/evaluation/**/INDEX*.md
AUDIO/evaluation/**/*.wav
AUDIO/evaluation/**/*.mp3
AUDIO/evaluation/**/*.flac
AUDIO/evaluation/**/*.zip

